          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "Super Kick Off is a football game for the Sega Mega Drive, Sega Master System and Sega Game Gear, released exclusively in Europe and Brazil. It is considered by many to be the watered-down version of Kick Off 2, previously released for the Commodore Amiga (and ported to the Amstrad CPC, Atari ST and Commodore 64). Kick Off 2 was originally programmed by Dino Dini for Anco Games, with the console adaptions being handled by Tiertex.\n\nFrom a franchise perspective, Super Kick Off would be followed by the controversial Kick Off 3: European Challenge. However, Dino Dini, who had no involvement in Kick Off 3 would go on to form his own company and produce the Amiga/IBM PC game Goal!, which shares similar gameplay. Goal! also arrived on the Mega Drive, in the updated form of Dino Dini's Soccer.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary_es",
          "value": "Super Kick Off es un juego de fútbol para Sega Mega Drive, Sega Master System y Sega Game Gear, lanzado exclusivamente en Europa y Brasil. Muchos lo consideran una versión simplificada de Kick Off 2, lanzado previamente para Commodore Amiga (y adaptado a Amstrad CPC, Atari ST y Commodore 64). Kick Off 2 fue programado originalmente por Dino Dini para Anco Games, y las adaptaciones para consola fueron realizadas por Tiertex.\n\nDesde el punto de vista de la franquicia, Super Kick Off fue seguido por el polémico Kick Off 3: European Challenge. Sin embargo, Dino Dini, que no participó en Kick Off 3, fundó su propia compañía y produjo el juego Goal! para Amiga y PC IBM, de jugabilidad similar. Goal! también llegó a Mega Drive, en su versión actualizada, como Dino Dini's Soccer.",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "year",
          "value": "1991",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        }
      ],
