    {
      "id": 761,
      "nameEs": "Kick Off 3: European Challenge",
      "originalName": "Kick Off 3: European Challenge",
      "year": 1994,
      "igdbId": 45708,
      "popularity": 0,
      "iconic": false,
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "name_es",
          "value": "Kick Off 3: European Challenge",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "original_name",
          "value": "Kick Off 3: European Challenge",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "Kick Off 3: European Challenge is a football game developed by Steve Screech for Anco Games as a sequel to Kick Off 2 (which made it to the Sega Mega Drive in the altered form of Super Kick Off). VIC Tokai published a version for the Mega Drive in 1994.\n\nUnlike its predecessors, Kick Off 3 had no involvement from lead programmer Dino Dini, and thus plays very differently to other games in the series, having a \"horizontal\" pitch as opposed to a \"vertical\" one. Due to these radical changes, the game was met with controversy upon release. Dino Dini released his own football game around the same time for the Amiga titled Goal!, which made its way onto the Mega Drive as Dino Dini's Soccer.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary_es",
          "value": "Kick Off 3: European Challenge es un juego de fútbol desarrollado por Steve Screech para Anco Games como secuela de Kick Off 2 (que llegó a Sega Mega Drive en la versión alterada Super Kick Off). VIC Tokai publicó una versión para Mega Drive en 1994.\n\nA diferencia de sus predecesores, Kick Off 3 no contó con la participación del programador principal Dino Dini, por lo que se juega de forma muy distinta a otros juegos de la serie, con un campo «horizontal» en lugar de uno «vertical». Debido a estos cambios radicales, el juego generó controversia al salir. Dino Dini lanzó por esas fechas su propio juego de fútbol para Amiga, Goal!, que llegó a Mega Drive como Dino Dini's Soccer.",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "year",
          "value": "1994",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        }
      ],
